The contract contains a critical vulnerability where the close_remainder_to field in payment transactions is not properly validated, allowing complete account drainage.

### Vulnerability: Unchecked Close Remainder To
### Explanation: The contract fails to validate that the close_remainder_to field in the payment transaction (Gtxn[2]) is set to the zero address. This allows an attacker to specify any arbitrary address in the close_remainder_to field, which would result in the entire remaining balance of the account being sent to that address when the transaction is executed.
### Risk: Critical - Complete loss of all remaining ALGOs in the account
